                <pb facs="0066" n="59" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg59"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/1586: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davies</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-26T19:00:00+03:00">March 26, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 26—2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Am advised by Chinese Ambassador at Moscow that his Government and U. S. S.
                    R. have arrived at a definite agreement providing that the U. S. S. R. will not
                    support or encourage communistic groups or communistic armies or independent
                    states against present Chinese Government and that Chinese Government continue
                    support such groups through absorption in or through government activities.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davies</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
